From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:53:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] port f8fcc276: serve: ConvCacheLog counts the borrow
 lines ("borrowed N tokens from a parked conversation", "borrowed N of a
 parked M-token conversation") and "restored N of M tokens"

(cherry picked from commit f8fcc2762e01d10a9c73e4e055be7df2826ff92a, re-applied by hand)

Adaptations: v0.2.12's engine writes its own one-GPU borrow line ("borrowed N tokens from a parked conversation,
which stays parked, in X ms; parked=P bytes=B borrowed=K"), which the old EVENT pattern did not count either; the
same pattern now counts it (restores and borrows), beside our split borrow line (now ending "checkpoints=C
borrowed=K") and the "restored N of M tokens" line of STRATA_PARK_BORROW=1.  The docstring names all three.
test_conv_cache_borrow: ours, plus upstream's borrow line and its "cannot borrow" / "no room beside" lines, which
must not count.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
